051890444415,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":49.7,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.12477124948363966,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.23858,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Ardent Health, Inc. owns and operates a network of hospitals and clinics that provides healthcare services in the United States. The company offers general and specialty services, including internal medicine, general surgery, cardiology, oncology, orthopedics, women's services, neurology, urology, and emergency services within inpatient and ambulatory care settings. It also operates a network of ambulatory facilities and telehealth services, including primary care and specialty care clinics, ambulatory surgery centers, urgent care centers, free-standing emergency departments, and diagnostic imaging centers. The company operates acute care hospitals, including rehabilitation hospitals and surgical hospitals. Ardent Health, Inc. was formerly known as Ardent Health Partners, Inc. and changed its name to Ardent Health, Inc. in June 2025. The company was founded in 2001 and is based in Brentwood, Tennessee. Ardent Health, Inc. is a subsidiary of EGI-AM Investments, L.L.C.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David  Caspers | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $324K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $13K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Ardent Health, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.5B market cap on $6.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 8% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $259M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.46\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 24% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.6pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5273173726212406},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 12% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 72% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 43% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Ardent Health (ARDT) Lifts Guidance And Earnings, Is The Upside Already Priced In?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nyse-ardt/ardent-health/news/ardent-health-ardt-lifts-guidance-and-earnings-is-the-upside","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794450370.458,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.977,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"What Ardent Health (ARDT) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/what-ardent-health-ardt-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794233579.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.784,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (ARDT) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.st